"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: A Chrome 159 measured corpus for Devanagari (OpenType `dev2`) shaping,
written BEFORE the general shaper lands (TDD). Each `it` is one shaping rule
group; for every word it compares, on the `cpu_simd` lane, Simple's layout
width, rendered ink box and glyph ids with the Chrome values below.
Audience: web renderer text maintainers; the GSUB lane (syllables, reordering,
substitution) and the GPOS lane (mark positioning) use it as their target.

EXPECTED RED: on the base this spec was written against (release/1.0.0
ecff7320c13) only हिन्दी is admitted to the shaped path, so every group fails;
AC-1 (shaped already) is red only on its 16px ink top (28 vs Chrome 30). The spec is tagged `@tag:in-development` so a whole-suite run skips
and COUNTS it instead of turning red (doc/07_guide/infra/testing.md § Tags and
Filtering). Nothing is skipped inside the file: an explicit-path run executes
every group. Delete the tag in the commit that makes all groups green.

Chrome oracle (Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6, `--headless=new --disable-gpu
--force-device-scale-factor=1 --hide-scrollbars --window-size=400,300`,
`<html lang="hi">`, body `margin:0;background:#fff;color:#000;
font:<16|32>px Liberation Sans, <Noto Sans Devanagari via @font-face>` — the
face the engine resolves for `lang="hi"`:
`assets/fonts/google-fonts/ofl/notosansdevanagari/NotoSansDevanagari[wdth,wght].ttf`,
default instance), text in
`<div style="position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;white-space:nowrap">`.
- width: `Range.getBoundingClientRect().width` over the div's contents
  (LayoutUnit, exact multiples of 1/64 px; the spec stores width*64).
- ink: inclusive pixel box of pixels with any channel under 200 in the
  screenshot. The engine renders 400x120 (the div is absolutely positioned, so
  the viewport height does not move it; Chrome's lowest ink row is 68).
- glyph ids: from Chrome's `--print-to-pdf` output (Skia Type3 fonts keep the
  glyph id in the CharProc name), in visual order, at 16px. Glyph 3 (space) is
  what HarfBuzz leaves for a hidden ZWJ/ZWNJ; it is dropped on both sides.
The Range height is 17 (16px) / 36 (32px) and the div height 21 / 42 for every
row.

Tolerance: width within 1px (64/64), every ink edge within 1px, glyph ids
exact. A failure message lists each deviating word as
`<text>@<size> <what> got=<simple> want=<chrome>`.

| group | text | codepoints | glyph ids | width@16 | ink@16 x0,y0..x1,y1 | width@32 | ink@32 x0,y0..x1,y1 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
